  "2026-10-27T12:02:50.431Z",codex-agent,"Class audit complete. General rule: compare both source and stored values using the actual SDK writer semantics; transport complete tag tokens without changing their boundaries. The import no-op guard now resolves built-in, configured and active-extension type aliases through resolveItemTypeRegistry. All three closeout Epic eligibility predicates use that normalization, preserving readable legacy epic/EPIC data. Other type comparisons in the package are GitHub GraphQL/form/rule discriminators rather than SDK item types. Every generic tag write in SDK atomic import/refresh, CLI create/update/link, project import/push and exact identity removal now uses one lossless SDK-compatible codec. It retains CSV bytes when lossless and uses JSON arrays otherwise; stored tag arrays compare as literal tokens. Raw type input and ordinary wire bytes remain unchanged for durable transaction fingerprints. Plain import retains apply-each-time behavior; project status-only pull does not rewrite tags. No substantive non-blocking finding was supplied or found in the connected review receipts; skipped/quota-limited reviews are not approval.\n\nAdversarial acceptance passed 13/13, zero failures/skips/cancellations: real non-git trackers; 16 mixed new/native closed batches over type aliases and label corpora; pairwise delimiter/JSON/Unicode/prototype-key tag transport; atomic and plain provider links; refresh; project import/push/conflicts; legacy Epic exclusion; exact identity removal; packed npm and native Bun in JSON/TOON, including plain create/update. Command: node --test --test-concurrency=2 --test-name-pattern=\"tag transport property|mixed closed imports|additive provider links|packed npm|apply then re-apply|project sync applies draft|project sync resolves simultaneous|project import preserves literal|identity repair removes exact|legacy type casing\" test/import-projection.test.ts test/refresh.test.ts test/project-sync.test.ts test/identity.test.ts test/closeout.test.ts. Build and build:test passed.\n\nBehavioral revert proof: restoring ONLY normalizeImportValue() from af84be5 fails both mixed closed-import byte stability and legacy type casing (2 tests, 0 passed, 2 failed). Command: node --test --test-concurrency=2 --test-name-pattern=\"mixed closed imports|legacy type casing\" test/import-projection.test.ts test/closeout.test.ts. Restoring ONLY pre-fix CSV transport in serializeImportTags() fails 7 of 9 class checks (2 pass, 7 fail), including transport property, mixed batch, additive provider, refresh in both modes, project push and identity removal; the two status-only conflict tests correctly still pass. Command: node --test --test-concurrency=2 --test-name-pattern=\"tag transport property|mixed closed imports|additive provider links|apply then re-apply|project sync applies draft|project sync resolves simultaneous|identity repair removes exact\" test/import-projection.test.ts test/refresh.test.ts test/project-sync.test.ts test/identity.test.ts. Both restorations were reverted before final verification. The latest instruction requires both full gates, superseding the earlier CI-only handoff; running serially with at most two workers."
