  "2026-10-27T16:43:54.993Z",codex-agent,"Round-2 resolution class audit and proof: all core settings and type/status registries now come from readGithubWorkspace(), which calls public resolvePmRoot(cwd, input) before readSettings(), resolveItemTypeRegistry() and resolveRuntimeStatusRegistry(). Import, fidelity finalization, refresh planning/apply, issue-form binding, closeout, export/sync, project push/pull/import, blocker selection and changelog filtering share canonical names or configured lifecycle roles. Atomic settings injection already receives the SDK-resolved tracker. Refresh resolves the source root first and derives registries inside its disposable read copy, preserving read-only previews. Authenticated webhook storage now uses resolvePmRoot plus ensureTrackerInitialized, replacing its raw settings-file read. Remaining type/status comparisons are provider/form discriminators, HTTP/process statuses and SDK journal states, not native item fields. Ordinary import option bytes remain unchanged for existing journal fingerprints.\n\nThe pinned SDK public declarations provide resolvePmRoot(cwd, cliPath), readSettings(pmRoot), resolveItemTypeRegistry(settings, registrations), resolveRuntimeStatusRegistry(schema), normalizeStatusInput(value, registry) and isTerminalStatus(value, registry). getWorkspaceContracts exposes canonical lists but not alias maps. These core public APIs suffice; no extension section or raw settings file is read. The separate missing extension-owned-section reader is documented by unbraind/pm-cli#1580, and is not bypassed here.\n\nFocused acceptance: 98/98 passed across test/workspace-resolution.test.ts, test/import-projection.test.ts, test/projects.test.ts, test/refresh.test.ts and test/project-sync.test.ts using node --test --test-concurrency=2. Includes 16 real mixed closed batches, nested workspace/tracker/relative path forms, custom type probe -> Investigation, custom active/terminal status aliases, exact item/history bytes, native SDK 